  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 102 PM MDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nA week boundary pushes down the plains, and the heat dome pushes a \nbit farther south. This should be enough to allow more widespread \nconvection over the entire region. Additionally, it will be  a bit \ncooler this day as 700 mb temps cool down a few degrees. Since the \nplume is over us any storm on this day will have the potential to \nproduce localized heavy rain. Precip is expected to last into the \nnighttime hours.\n\nFor Wednesday, a weak wave moving over the ridge will flatten it \nsomewhat a bit of upper level forcing will assist with storm \ncoverage this day. Deterministic guidance along with the statistical \nguidance products show potential for heavier precip over the mtns \nand I-25 corridor regions on this day, especially late afternoon and \nevening hours. Temperatures may actually reach down to seasonable \nvalues this day although it may be rather humid by Colorado \nstandards. \n\nFor the rest of the week, ridge tries to rebuild over the region so \nstorm potential on the plains will lessen and temps at lower \nelevations will likely increase upward once again. However the \nmoisture plume will still be over the higher terrain, and this \nshould allow for the continuations of afternoon storms over the mtns.\n\nhopefully the long range products verify for NEXT week as the heat \ndome is fcst to flatten out and we may actually get some cooler air \ndown this way. \\/Hodanish",
